www.meetup.com/forest-footprints/events/316232035/","description":"Once a year, we get to be whoever—or whatever—we want! 😈✨\nMasks, costumes, makeup, crazy characters… Halloween is our excuse to step out of everyday life and have some fun!\n\nSo… who do YOU want to be this Halloween? 🧙‍♀️🧛‍♂️🦸‍♀️👻\n\nLet’s gather our hiking crew, put on our wildest costumes, eat, drink, dance, laugh, and party like there’s no tomorrow! 💃🕺🎶\n\n📍 Location: Tehroon 60 Restaurant\n📅 Date: November 6\n⏰ Time: 7:00–11:00 PM\n💰 Entry: $30\n🍹 Includes light dinner\n🍽️ Order your own drink\n\n🎟️ Save your spot: E-transfer $30 to\nmojgan.mn@hotmail.com\n\nAnd remember… the crazier the costume, the better! 🎭😂\n\nCome ready to leave your everyday self at the door and let your Halloween character take over for one night! 🎃🥳\n\nLet’s make this a night to remember! 🥂💃🕺","startDate":"2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Tehroon 60 restaurant","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Richmond hill","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"12963 Yonge st,, Richmond hill, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Forest Footprints","url":"https://www.meetup.com/forest-footprints/"},"performer":"Forest Footprints"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Mississauga- let’s speak French/ Parlons français","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/314155028/","description":"Let’s get together to speak French! We’ll enjoy tea/coffee and some icebreaker games. Everyone is welcome.\n\nVenez parler français!\n\nÀ bientôt,\n\nHassane.\n\n\\*Merci beaucoup de vous être inscrit(e) à notre prochaine rencontre! Nous sommes ravis de votre présence.\nAfin de permettre à d’autres de se joindre à nous, nous vous demandons respectueusement :\n\n1. **Si vos plans changent,** veuillez mettre à jour votre statut (passer à 'Non') le plus rapidement possible pour libérer votre place.\n2. **Si vous êtes sur la liste d'attente,** merci de ne pas vous présenter à l'événement. Votre statut doit être confirmé pour pouvoir participer. Veuillez vous inscrire directement aux prochaines dates disponibles.\n\nAu plaisir de vous accueillir!\n\n\\*To allow others to join us, we respectfully ask that you:\n\n* **If your plans change,** please update your RSVP status (change it to 'No') as quickly as possible to free up your spot.\n* **If you are on the waiting list,** please do not show up for the event. Your status must be confirmed to participate. Instead, please register directly for the next available dates.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nVeuillez noter que pour profiter pleinement de nos échanges, une aptitude de base à la conversation est vivement souhaitée : ce groupe est un cercle de discussion convivial et non un cours de langue.\n\nPlease note that to fully enjoy the experience, a basic speaking aptitude is recommended: this group is a social conversation circle, not a formal teaching class.\n\nWe look forward to welcoming you!\n\nPlease join our WhatsApp group:\n\nhttps://chat.whatsapp.com/LRUdXbjpG8I9aph4dU6Go8","startDate":"2026-11-06T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Chocolate and love cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"5985 Rodeo Dr Unit 14, Mississauga, ON L5R 3V6,, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Casual Board Games and Pub Social After","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/events/316441942/","description":"The Board Games event is a fun, sociable and charitable event\n\nWe are a fun, friendly and kind group of people mostly in our 20s, 30s and 40s. Beginners are welcome! We are a very inclusive and social group and we teach people how to play games they have not played before :)\n\nWe provide a variety of 40+ board games. The games usually take 5 or 10 minutes to learn and 30 to 60 minutes to play.\n\nPlay in French: On the last Friday of the month, we're offering a table where the games are played in French. Anyone with an intermediate level of French who wants to practice while playing is welcome to join. Just ask for Philippe when you arrive.\n\n**Time**\n\n*Board Games Start time: 630pm\n- Board Games end time: 10pm\n*Eat / Drink/ Socialise at a nearby pub afterwards\n\n**Location**\n\n30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8 (Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection)\n\nThe entrance to the board game room is at the back of the Church. There is a sign on the door that says BOARD GAMES GROUP.\n\nPlease use the map provided on the event page also.\n\nPayment\n**There are two ways to pay**\n**10 by Cash - coins are not accepted. Only bills.****\n**11.55 by Debit/Credit card\n\n**Charity Donations**\n\n- This is a not-for-profit initiative. Revenue go towards covering costs of the event including venue, insurance marketing, refreshments and board games. Any surplus revenue is donated to charity\n\n**Food and drink**\n\n*Everyone will get cookies/candy for free\n- Cups will be provided for tap water\n*Bring your own food and drink.\n- Please do not bring CHIPS AND CRACKERS as they make a mess and are greasy\n***ALCOHOL IS PROHIBITED AND WE HAVE A ZERO TOLERANCE POLICY ON THIS - there are no second chances**\n\nPhotos will be taken at the event and posted publicly for marketing purposes. Please only attend if you are ok with this or tell me when you arrive that you do not want to be in any photos\n\nThe event is officially hosted by Ace of Math Learning Program Ontario Inc.","startDate":"2026-11-06T23:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Board Games and Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/"},"performer":"Board Games and Social"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎤 Toronto Karaoke Night – Every Friday at Ace of Spades Lounge 🎶","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/events/316702860/","description":"Looking for a fun Friday night in Toronto? Join us **every Friday at 8:00 PM** for an unforgettable **Karaoke Night** at **Ace of Spades Lounge**!\nWhether you're a seasoned performer or just want to cheer on your friends, everyone is welcome. Grab the mic, sing your favorite songs, meet new people, and enjoy a night full of great energy.\n\n### What to Expect\n\n🎤 Karaoke all night long\n🍔 Delicious food and late-night bites\n🍹 Great drinks from our full bar\n🤝 Meet new people and socialize\n🎶 Fun music and an exciting atmosphere\n✨ Good vibes and unforgettable memories\nCome solo, bring a date, or gather your friends—this is one of the best ways to kick off your weekend in Toronto.\n\n**📅 Every Friday**\n**🕗 Starts at 8:00 PM**\n**📍 Ace of Spades Lounge**\n536 Manning Avenue\nToronto, ON\n\n**🎙️ Grab the mic. Be the star.**\n**Come socialize, sing, eat, drink, and have fun—we'll see you every Friday!**","startDate":"2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Ace of Spades","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"536 Manning Ave., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/"},"performer":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Diwali Mini Market","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-nqiklspv/events/316651527/","description":"🪔 Diwali Mini-Market — The Festival of Lights ✨\n\nJoin The Cultural Gully for a vibrant celebration of Diwali and South Asian culture at Innovation Works in London, Ontario!\n\nCome celebrate the Festival of Lights with a lively mini-market featuring local vendors, delicious South Asian food and drinks, festive shopping, and a welcoming community atmosphere. Discover unique finds, connect with others, and enjoy an evening celebrating the richness and diversity of South Asian cultures and traditions.\n\nEveryone is welcome! Whether you celebrate Diwali or are simply curious to learn, connect, and enjoy the festivities, we invite people of all cultural backgrounds, ages, and communities to join us. Come as you are and celebrate the spirit of light, community, and togetherness. 🪔✨\n\n📅 Friday, November 6\n📍 Innovation Works, 201 King Street, London, ON\n🎟️ Free Entry\n\nBring your family, friends, and community for an evening filled with culture, connection, food, shopping, and celebration!\n\nA special thank you to the Inclusive Community Events Program from Pillar Nonprofit Network for their generous support in helping make this celebration possible. 💛\n\nCome celebrate with us — all are welcome! ✨🪔","startDate":"2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","